WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.930
- [Jared McCain:] I feel like people get mixed up a lot.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:05.190
They think I’m not locked in,
or I'm just doing TikTok,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.947
but, you know, it's so different.

00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:10.427
[Indistinct shouts]

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:11.825
[Upbeat music]

00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:12.907
♪ Hear me girl ♪

00:00:12.907 --> 00:00:15.389
♪ I remember when you ♪

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:17.972
[Mellow music]

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.297
Come on.

00:00:24.297 --> 00:00:27.519
♪♪

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:28.840
- The thing that I think sets Jared apart

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.030
is from the time he came in as a freshmen,

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.530
his work ethic—

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.270
and there's a lot of
people that work hard—

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.460
but I would say it was
his attention to detail

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.466
in how he worked.

00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:40.133
♪♪

00:00:42.847 --> 00:00:44.340
- The drive just comes from my main goal,

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.457
which is to make it to the NBA.

00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:48.210
I mean, that's been my goal
since I was three years old

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.210
when I first started playing basketball.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.440
And since I'm not there yet,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.995
then I can't really stop working.

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:56.724
♪♪

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:59.775
You know, I'm a TikToker, but I'll
still give you buckets.

00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:00.608
[Laughing]

00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:05.608
[Hip-hop music]
[Indistinct chatter]

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.025
Why would you leave me open?

00:01:16.025 --> 00:01:20.493
[Hip-hop music]
[Indistinct chatter]

00:01:20.493 --> 00:01:22.576
[Cheering]

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.830
Peach Jam is when I feel
like I blew up the most.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.450
I was, you know,
combining with the TikToks

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.322
before every game.

00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:31.945
♪ Yeah, I'm in New York counting shmoney ♪

00:01:31.945 --> 00:01:33.735
♪ Yeah, ain’t the stuntman,
but I'm stuntin' ♪

00:01:33.735 --> 00:01:35.763
♪ It's eight o'clock in the morning ♪

00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:37.615
♪ Now I'm entering my bed ♪

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.248
Here, here, here.

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.300
[Laughing]

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.850
Yeah, you can't mess it up, JJ.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.570
I wrote down my goals for Peach Jam

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.250
and I achieved every single one.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.840
We won Peach Jam and I
averaged 20, five and five.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.465
So I was able to just do
what I can do and show out,

00:01:54.465 --> 00:01:55.900
and I won MVP.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.409
I think Peach Jam was when I
really put everyone on notice.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:01.492
[Indistinct chatter]

00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.491
Nice shot, Jared.

00:02:07.491 --> 00:02:08.750
What up, what up, what?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.560
I started, like, really
taking basketball serious

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.700
my eighth-grade year,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.370
training with my trainer every
day after school and stuff.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.540
And I was able to start on varsity,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.190
which was like a blessing for me.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.903
And so from then on, I just
started working every day.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.330
I would describe my game, I feel like,

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.550
I'm just gonna make
the right play every time.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:26.383
I'm a great shooter.

00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:28.385
I can, if you're gonna pass me the ball,

00:02:28.385 --> 00:02:29.290
I'm probably going to get that thing up,

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.363
and most likely it's going in.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.743
[Sneakers squealing]

00:02:34.743 --> 00:02:36.820
The TikTok, I feel like a
lot of people come at me.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:37.830
I think it's more fun.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.140
It's like they're coming at you

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.573
and you're still killing them.

00:02:42.438 --> 00:02:45.130
[Sneakers squeaking]

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.297
Oh.

00:02:46.297 --> 00:02:47.437
[Clapping]

00:02:47.437 --> 00:02:48.340
I'm just an athlete.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.910
You can obviously find a
balance between having fun,

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:51.850
being mindful of yourself

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.027
and then just being a dog on the court.

00:02:53.027 --> 00:02:55.010
- Our pressure needs to be
different than everybody else's.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.580
No matter how many people
are in there or not,

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:57.730
we bring our own energy.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.563
We do all that stuff.
We're going to crank it up.

00:02:59.563 --> 00:03:01.490
Make sure we're pressuring the
ball from the very beginning.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.520
Any questions with that?

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.230
I think his basketball
IQ is off the charts.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.420
- Setting the screen going this way...

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.750
- If he's going that way—

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.870
- That's where I tag.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.650
But if he's going this way. Is
that me, or is that Ramsey?

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:11.690
- If he's going away from you,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.256
- Yeah, that's me.
- you'll stagger,

00:03:13.256 --> 00:03:14.210
and then you got to recover back.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.850
- OK.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.440
- [Giles:] If he's not the smartest
player I've ever coached,

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.739
he's up there in the top two or three.

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:23.198
[Sneakers squeaking]

00:03:23.198 --> 00:03:24.700
[Whistle blowing]
- And-1.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.010
- He does a really good job
of understanding, on offense,

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.730
how to let the game come to him,

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.010
finding open spots.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.320
The other teams,
they kind of know who he is,

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.810
so defensively he gets
a lot of attention.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.700
It doesn't frustrate
him. He stays within it,

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.040
stays within the game.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.030
And then, you know,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.870
I talk a lot about making
the right basketball play;

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.573
he makes the right basketball
play the majority of the time.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.950
I think there's a lot of players—

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.030
elite players—that could learn
a lot by watching him play

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.214
because he plays the right way.

00:03:54.214 --> 00:03:57.297
[Chatter]

00:03:58.814 --> 00:03:59.647
- They won, right?

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.694
- They don't look like they won.

00:04:01.694 --> 00:04:03.254
[Clapping]

00:04:03.254 --> 00:04:04.454
- Let's go. "Family" on
three. One, two, three.

00:04:04.454 --> 00:04:05.287
- [All:] Family.

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:06.860
- Yeah, before the game, I'm usually just—

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.580
there's always butterflies for
me, just nervous every game.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.320
But once you get on
the court, it's nothing.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.300
Everything kind of goes away.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.010
But before the game, I just get locked in.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.290
I read my book that I
read before every game.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.180
It's called "The Inner Game of Tennis."

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.870
And, you know, it just puts
me in the right mindset.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.537
[Hip hop music]

00:04:24.552 --> 00:04:26.553
- "Execute" on three. One, two, three.

00:04:26.553 --> 00:04:27.386
[Horn buzzing]

00:04:27.386 --> 00:04:29.570
- Mental side is one of the biggest things,

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.370
if not the most important
thing, I feel like.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.964
I'm obviously not the
most athletic player.

00:04:33.964 --> 00:04:34.940
You can't guard me, boy.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.690
Getting an edge any way,
for me, was mental.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.790
So, just knowing that I can
stay positive during the game

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.360
and just keeping my
calm, never get too high,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.564
never get too low.

00:04:42.564 --> 00:04:44.980
♪♪

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.280
During the game, I'm just locked in to

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.830
whatever Coach tells me

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:48.730
and just locked in to winning.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.060
That's really the main thing for all this,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.650
no matter how many points
are scored ever.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.953
Just winning the game is the main thing.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.450
Jalen Green has done
this a couple of times,

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.070
so just to be in the mix with those names,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:05.078
it's amazing to represent California at Hoophall.

00:05:05.078 --> 00:05:07.745
♪♪

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.370
"Soft" is really the main word they use

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.310
for California basketball.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.130
But I think we're just really
skilled players out there.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.273
I feel like shooting is
a California thing, too.

00:05:17.273 --> 00:05:19.856
♪♪

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.210
My main goal for basketball—

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.280
I feel like I've already
started to do it a little bit—

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.541
but just to inspire kids
to just keep working.

00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:28.920
You know, I'm not the most athletic kid.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.240
I'm not doing all these crazy dunks.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.447
But I just continue to
work, and I continue to work

00:05:33.447 --> 00:05:34.991
in inspiring in anything,

00:05:34.991 --> 00:05:37.793
whether it's basketball
or something else in the world.

00:05:37.793 --> 00:05:39.652
You know that ball don't lie.

00:05:39.652 --> 00:05:41.244
- No. 11 can come in transition,

00:05:41.244 --> 00:05:42.200
shoot the three. The point guard.
- OK.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.632
That's Shannon right now playing him?

00:05:43.632 --> 00:05:44.570
- Yeah.
- OK.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.190
That's the one who's
kind of cocky—

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.582
- "Family" on three. One, two, three.
- [All:] Family.

00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:51.249
♪♪

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.250
- [Giles:] For Jared's future,

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.513
I think Jared can accomplish
just about anything he wants.
- [All:] Amen.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.340
- If he were to struggle,
or if he has a bad game,

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.790
or whatever it may be,

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.700
he will turn that into a motivator,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.980
and he will become so
much better because of it.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.647
[Chatter]

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.070
- Overall, the event was good

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:18.480
and we were able to come to South Dakota

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.450
and get the job done.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:20.600
Do what we had to do to win.

